course: dictionary
lesson: 809
title: Speaking for someone else
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Behalf is a noun, but you almost never meet it alone. You find it in phrases: on behalf of, on someone's behalf, and on my behalf. Each one means you are acting for another person, as their stand-in.
explain: «Liverpool held the 2023 contest on Ukraine's behalf.» Liverpool did the job in Ukraine's place, for Ukraine. To check, swap in your meaning: "Liverpool held the contest as Ukraine's stand-in." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: The same phrase is used when one person speaks for a group. «On behalf of the class, thank you.» The speaker is not thanking only for themselves; they are thanking everyone. You will often see it in formal letters too, written before a name.
fact: Behalf is a noun, and it is used almost only in the phrases on behalf of and on someone's behalf.
fact: «On behalf of» means as a representative of someone, or in their place.
fact: «On behalf of» can also mean for the good of someone.
fact: In American English you may see «in behalf of», which means the same thing.
fact: «On my behalf» means for me, or in my place.
exercise: «The 2023 contest was held in Liverpool on Ukraine's behalf.» What does on behalf mean here? | Very near to Ukraine | Against Ukraine, to beat them | Under Ukraine's flag only | *In the place of Ukraine, as its stand-in
exercise: Ayo stands up and says, «On behalf of the class, thank you.» Who is Ayo thanking? | Only himself | The teacher alone, and nobody else | The class's pet hamster | *Everyone in the class, as their speaker
exercise: Which phrase means "for me, in my place"? | *on my behalf | on my own | in my pocket | at my side
test: In «She signed the letter on behalf of her parents», what does on behalf of mean? | Against her parents' wishes | *As a stand-in for her parents, in their place | Because her parents were tired | Without her parents knowing
test: Which phrase fits the gap? «The head teacher spoke ___ the whole school at assembly.» | by behalf of | *on behalf of | for behalf | at behalf to
exam: What does «He accepted the prize on behalf of his sister, who was ill» mean? | *He accepted it as a stand-in for his sister | He took the prize for himself | He accepted it only because it was shiny | He gave the prize away to a stranger
